    11	# Kaggriculture grammar heads sit behind Isaiah's actor projection
    12	
    13	## What changed (rebuild Task 2.3, brief v3)
    14	
    15	- **Topology.** `actor_input_proj = nn.Linear(3D, D)` over `[entity ‖ self player ‖ plan]`, as Isaiah's `source_actor_input_proj`. The market queue has no entity, so it uses `[plan ‖ player ‖ plan]`. `KaggricultureGrammarActor` (`python/owl/model/kaggriculture_actor.py`) holds everything game-specific:
    16	  - `source_norm`
    17	  - `market_position` (11 = 10 queue slots plus the forced sentinel)
    18	  - seven prefix `slot_embeddings`
    19	  - nine `OutputProjectionMLP` heads, one per sampled slot
    20	
    21	  Stage input is `base + prefix / sqrt(stage + 1)`, and the prefix resets for every observation. The reference model was a design and test oracle only: it had a `prefix_norm` and a factorized `frame_input`, and neither was taken.
    22	- **Tables.** `GrammarTables` (`python/owl/kaggriculture/gpu_grammar.py`) holds the eight Task 1.2 tables, with validation.
    23	  - `expected_grammar_tables()` re-derives them from the brief's support rules.
    24	  - `native_grammar_tables()` is the named hook for the Task 1.2/1.4 binding. It raises `NotImplementedError` until then.
    25	  - The model defaults to the expected tables and keeps them as non-persistent buffers, so they never enter checkpoints.
    26	- **Sampling.** Exact Gumbel-max throughout. `couple_market_kinds` implements the HIRE correction: the raw-HIRE prefix masks HIRE where capacity is exhausted, and the argmax is re-taken over the same perturbed scores. Densities use the final-HIRE prefix. STOP is the first final NONE, which keeps its slot-7 density; the sentinel has zero density.
    27	- **Replay.** `evaluate_actions` runs the same core, teacher-forced.
    28	  - Python shape and dtype checks run before any kernel.
    29	  - Every replay-derived index is clamped to a temporary value, and its validity goes into the flags.
    30	  - Three flag groups: support, length and canonical equality.
    31	  - `check_replay_flags` makes one compact host transfer and raises `GrammarReplayError`, naming the groups and the first failing row.
    32	  - Sampling adds no policy-validation host synchronization: `forward` never runs the replay check. The encode is not sync-free: packed trunk dispatch sizes its packing on the host (Isaiah's `build_packed_sequence`), and an oversized packed batch transfers per-row token counts to plan chunks. (Corrected after Codex's Task 2.3 verification, `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/codex/verify-2.3-r1.md`.)
    33	- **Outputs.** `event [E,2,252,12]`, `per_player_entity = event.sum(-1)`, zero `launch`, per-slot entropy `components`, and critic values from the same encode.
    34	- **Initialization and optimizer.** The embedding `.weight`s are in `get_input_layers` (std `D^-0.5`). Every `head.out` is in `get_output_layers` with gain 0.01; `reset_parameters` now follows Isaiah's output-layer loop. `actor_input_proj` and every head `.up` go to Muon.
    35	- **Overflow guards (brief §9):**
    36	  - `trunk_gemm_width`: the max of `max(in, out)` over every trunk Linear, enumerated by a test.
    37	  - The packed trunk path chunks at row boundaries (`packed_row_chunks`) instead of raising.
    38	  - `head_rows_per_chunk` keeps `rows × 252 × max(3D, D, widest head) < 2^31` (11,096 rows at D = 256).
    39	  - The heads stay eager in production.
    40	- **Size.** 6,252,223 parameters at the preset: encoder 5,312,768, critic 66,049, heads 873,406. That is inside the owner's 6–10M budget, so the depth stays 8.
    41	
    42	## Checks
    43	
    44	- `OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 uv run pytest tests/kaggriculture -q`: 256 passed, 1 skipped (the native-table comparison, which waits for Task 1.2).
    45	- `just py-prepare`: Ruff and mypy clean, 979 passed with 4 skips. Docs freshness passes with the mapped docs updated.
    46	- Brief §7 items 1–10 have tests:
    47	  1. saved-sample replay (whole, split, permuted) for the dense, HIRE-capacity, STOP-at-every-position and mixed/inactive cases, to ≤ 1e-5
    48	  2. every table row, plus the quantity cases, through both the tables and replay
    49	  3. Gumbel chi-square over 20k draws
    50	  4. enumeration of the actual `couple_market_kinds` against the replayed densities at budgets 0/1/2/3/10 (FP64, 1e-9, NONE and EMPTY corrections)
    51	  5. STOP and marginalization
    52	  6. every malformed group, including out-of-range indices with no fault
    53	  7. an `eager`/`fullgraph=True` captured core, plus an FP64 finite difference
    54	  8. seat isolation and statelessness
    55	  9. topology, initialization and Muon membership
    56	  10. the budget
    57	
    58	  Item 11 is skipped with its reason.
    59	- Deliberate mutations, each restored byte-for-byte (SHA-256 checked):
    60	  - a batch-mean term in the market input fails the replay invariant (4 cases)
    61	  - an inclusive raw-HIRE prefix fails the enumeration (3 budgets)
    62	  - dropping the actor-ordinal slot from canonical equality fails 2 canonical cases
    63	  - dropping the head outputs from `get_output_layers` fails the Muon and initialization tests
    64	- Codex's independent verification of `0e989a1..5ec3af1` (`ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/codex/verify-2.3-heads/report.md`) found no functional defect and approved with one wording edit, applied above. It reran `tests/kaggriculture` (256 passed, 1 skipped) and the full non-slow suite (979 passed, 4 skipped), and three further mutations (raw replay index, partial canonical equality, inclusive raw-HIRE prefix) each failed their tests. Market-position noise independence inside `policy_core` is established by source inspection, not by a dedicated test.
    65	- Everything ran on CPU at tiny shapes. BF16, CUDA and a real compile are not qualified here; that is Phase 6.
    66	
    67	## Limits and reopening conditions
    68	
    69	- The masks come from synthetic tables until Task 1.2/1.4 exposes `kaggriculture_grammar_tables`. Then implement `native_grammar_tables`, switch the model default, and let `test_native_tables_match_expected_tables` run. Brief item 11 (recorded reference programs) also waits for 1.2.
    70	- The actor count is the own `actor_mask` sum, which assumes own actors fill slots `0..n-1` in frame order, as the contract and fixture do. `can_act` is not read by the heads.
    71	- The prefix embeddings (std `D^-0.5`) are added to a LayerNorm-scaled base with no second norm, as the brief specifies. At initialization the prefix signal is about `1/sqrt(D)` of the base. Whether this conditions strongly enough is untested; reopen if per-slot KL or BC accuracy shows weak item/quantity conditioning on kind.
    72	- The unit input materializes `[rows, 241, 3D]`, which is about 0.8 GB FP32 at 1,024 rows. The reference's factorized projection is mathematically equivalent if memory binds (Phase 6).
    73	- Trainer integration, factory registration (Task 3.1) and the startup workload assertion (Task 3.4) remain open.

