   716	no-grad teacher pass) is retained and is bit-for-bit equivalent to the cached
   717	path. The cached action-KL path supports only the discrete_targets actor without
   718	player-count adapters; a fixed teacher (`rl.teacher_mode: fixed`) must
   719	additionally share the student's launch mode. Value distillation
   720	(`rl.teacher_value_coef` > 0) only uses the critic winner distribution and does
   721	not require actor KL support, but the trainer still requires matching action
   722	specs and non-adapter models. `evaluate_action_kl(...)` remains as a
   723	compatibility path, but PPO updates do not use it. The KL comparison uses the
   724	same masks and factorization gates used by PPO replay. Non-acting source rows
   725	contribute zero KL. For binary discrete-target launch mode, no-launch replay
   726	rows include only the Bernoulli launch KL; target and fleet-size KL are computed
   727	only for rows where the replayed action launched. Discrete target-bin KL
   728	compares the target categorical and the selected target's fleet-bin categorical.
   729	Pure-action KL compares launch, marginal angle, and selected fleet-size
   730	distributions for launched rows. Angle KL is a permutation-invariant numerical
   731	integral over the marginal Von Mises mixture using component-centered
   732	quadrature points for each teacher angle component.
   733	
   734	Fleet-size KL is computed as the exact marginal KL between the selected
   735	truncated logistic mixture distributions over integer fleet sizes from
   736	`min_fleet_size` through the row's `max_launch`. The KL does not compare latent
   737	mixture identities, so component permutations between teacher and student are
   738	not penalized. Per-action KL portions are logged as components such as
