cookbook/references/ppo-trainer-seams-map-any-schema-and-alarm-on-replay-drift.md:55:- The raised `RuntimeError` reports the observed mean, the limit, the rollout `[segments, horizon, players]` shape, the minibatch width and every set observation tensor shape (the token counts), including action-mask tensors as `action_mask.can_act` and `action_mask.max_launch`, and it points to the compiler overflow Reference. Unset optional tensors are omitted.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:3:title: "Compiled GEMM template overflows above 2^21 rows"
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:4:description: "Torch 2.9 Inductor max-autotune Triton GEMM templates wrap the 32-bit A-load offset once rows × GEMM input width exceeds 2^31 while the size argument stays int32 (measured at widths 4096, 768 and 512 and silent in the real trunk; output-wide GEMMs stayed correct to 2^32); this caused the reference PPO-from-BC crash. The rebuilt trunk guard is measured correct at L−1 and rejects L; production compliance is unproven."
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:11:# Compiled GEMM template overflows above 2^21 rows
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:15:The reference branch's PPO run from the BC checkpoint crashed with a CUDA illegal memory access after 3 iterations. Rerunning the exact setup with `CUDA_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1` reproduced it on both ranks. Both tracebacks end in the Inductor **max-autotune Triton GEMM template** `triton_tem_fused__to_copy_addmm_gelu_t_view_9`, the transformer trunk's MLP with `M` = batch rows × tokens, K = 1024, N = 256. The kernel declares `INDEX_DTYPE = tl.int64`, which the mm template does not use, and forms the input-side offset `xindex = k + 1024*idx_m` in 32-bit arithmetic. Once `M > 2^21`, that offset passes 2³¹ and wraps. Here K = 1024 is the input width of the MLP down-projection.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:22:- The bug is in compiler-generated code, so it is invisible in the model source. It can reappear for any compiled GEMM whose `rows × input width` exceeds 2³¹: rollouts, evaluation, BC, and other models with larger batches. In training, backward reads forward outputs as inputs, so the forward output width counts too (below).
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:26:A second bounded probe compared compiled output against eager at every point. It covered synthetic compiled Linears and MLPs, plus the real `KaggricultureTransformer` trunk from `kg/rebuild-model` @ `1ddc71d`, compiled directly through its own `compile_transformer_trunk`. Precision matched `run_ppo`: fp32 parameters under bf16 autocast, `max-autotune-no-cudagraphs`, `dynamic=True`, compiled small first. Codex verified the evidence and requested edits, applied here. The table, the generated-code attribution and the source citations are in `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/results.md`, "GEMM limits at our shapes".
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:28:Measured (L_in = floor(2³¹ / K) for GEMM input width K, e.g. 2,796,202 for K = 768; trunk L = 2³¹/512 = 4,194,304):
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:29:- **The overflow is input-side at these shapes.** Input-wide GEMMs (4096→16, 768→256) were correct at L_in and failed at L_in+1. Output-wide GEMMs (16→4096, 256→512, 256→256) stayed correct up to M·N = 2³². The corrected kernel summaries show why:
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:34:  The earlier universal rule, "overflow iff M·max(K, N) > 2³¹", is withdrawn.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:48:- **Design bound: keep every compiled region at M × max(in, out) < 2³¹ over its Linear layers (the strict rule the guard implements; whether equality is safe on the real trunk was never measured).** This follows from the measured input-side rule plus backward: dX = dY·W reads dY at the forward output width, and weight-gradient GEMMs reduce over M. It is not justified by an output-store overflow.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:51:- **Production compliance is unproven.** Kaggriculture is not yet in `ModelConfig` or the model factory, and `configure_model_compile` rejects it for `model_compile="trunk"`. Integrated rollout, PPO recompute, evaluation, BC and teacher workloads stay unverified until Task 3.1 and Phase 6.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:52:- **Size margins against 2³¹/width, not against observed faults.** A passing test above the bound is not evidence of safety.
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:66:  - `bmm`, persistent-TMA and decompose-K paths (decompose-K is on by default and can apply to weight-gradient GEMMs);
cookbook/references/compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows.md:71:- **Other versions:** torch 2.8 showed no overflow at width 1024 (Task 0.2).
cookbook/references/index.md:20:- [[bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads|Native replay BC bootstrap]] — Market-disabled controls preserve3000 bank; exact admitted replay actions and Rust features support separate current-model BC, with episode holdout, two-rank smoke, observed overfitting and incomplete quality validation; automatic PPO disabled; BC stopped early for a separately requested PPO experiment, which then failed with a CUDA illegal memory access later traced to a compiler GEMM overflow; the planned architecture alignment schedules one BC rerun. Source review corrects omitted-unit handling: Python None is rejected, not encoded as NONE.
cookbook/references/index.md:21:- [[compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows|Compiled GEMM template overflows above 2^21 rows]] — Torch 2.9 Inductor max-autotune Triton GEMM templates wrap the 32-bit A-load offset once rows × input width exceeds 2^31 with an int32 size argument (measured at widths 4096/768/512, silent in the real trunk; output-wide GEMMs stayed correct to 2^32); design bound M × max(in, out) for training; trunk guard correct at L−1 and rejects L; production compliance unproven.
cookbook/references/index.md:22:- [[kaggriculture-encoder-reuses-isaiah-stateless-layers|Kaggriculture encoder reuses Isaiah's stateless layers]] — The rebuilt encoder uses Isaiah's StatelessTransformerV1 classes, token roles, packing, compile hook and initialization; only stem input widths are game-specific, and guards chunk both the padded and packed compiled GEMMs below 2^31. Describes the current tree.
cookbook/references/index.md:23:- [[kaggriculture-grammar-heads-sit-behind-isaiahs-actor-projection|Kaggriculture grammar heads sit behind Isaiah's actor projection]] — Task 2.3 adds the 3D→D actor projection and batched grammar heads with exact coupled-Gumbel HIRE sampling, same-path replay with support/length/canonical flags and one host check, head GEMM-extent chunking, and a 6,252,223-parameter preset; synthetic grammar tables stand in until Task 1.2. Describes the current tree.
cookbook/references/shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop.md:21:- The CUDA illegal memory access in the BC-initialized rollout is now explained: a Torch Inductor GEMM template overflows 32-bit offsets above 2^21 rows ([[compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows|compiler overflow Reference]]).
cookbook/references/native-game-semantics-use-v3-owned-buffers.md:35:The initial Python adapter reused checked int16/int32 action scratch arrays, mask-index tensors and the NumPy economic-counter view. When shaping is disabled it skips unnecessary float64 penalty arithmetic, retaining native cumulative counters and metrics. The regression suite includes narrowing-overflow rollback and replacement of subsequent actions.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:33:BC quality remains unqualified: the fixed held-out subset NLL reaches0.761 at14,600 updates, then degrades to1.954 at75,600 while training loss falls. This is overfitting on the selected corpus; longer runtime alone does not establish improvement. Best weights are retained. Full held-out evaluation, action-level fidelity and free-running economic behavior remain unverified. The owner subsequently requests a separate half-hour PPO from BC best; BC is stopped early for that switch, so there is no completed75-minute BC result. The separate launch is documented in `ops/ppo-from-bc-2026-09-29/plan.md`. It failed: after 3 iterations and only 6 optimizer steps (KL 1.8894/1.0453/0.3651; win rates 12.5/10.55/3.52% against the BC incumbent), rollout hit a CUDA illegal memory access and rank 1 then hit the 600 s NCCL timeout. A later blocking reproduction traced it to a compiler-generated GEMM overflow on the 8,192-row rollout forward, which also corrupted rollout activations. The KL spikes and falling win rates are therefore not evidence against the BC policy ([[compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows|compiler overflow Reference]]). No final checkpoint exists; the BC best and its pre-PPO copy have matching SHA-256. Automatic handoff remains disabled. The planned Isaiah alignment changes the architecture (per-player critic value tokens, possibly model size), so it schedules one BC rerun (`ops/gap-closure-2026-09-29/plan.md`, Phase 4). Preserve the [[../decisions/preserve-the-ppo-recipe-across-bc-bootstrap|PPO recipe]]; do not infer readiness or promotion from these local-loss smoke checks.

